update progressnote 
set description = 'Worker traveled to 3232 Rolling Road Edgewater, MD 21037 and completed a home visit. Present were Mr. Phipps and his children, Taylor and Hunter. During this visit Mr. Phipps expressed concerns about there being no safety plan and stated his children are not safe with their mother. Mr. Phipps stated Ms. Fox still lives with Mr. Kautz and stated that Ms. Fox will take the children to the house she shares with Mr. Kautz. Mr. Phipps said the children do not want to see their mother. Mr. Phipps stated he went to Anne Arundel County Circuit Court to obtain emergency custody but was denied. Mr. Phipps stated Taylor said she would run away if she had to return to her mother''s home. 

Worker explained to Mr. Phipps that when this worker spoke with Ms. Fox she was advised the children should have no contact with Mr. Kautz and that she could see her children at her mother''s residence. Worker asked Mr. Phipps why does he not want the children to have contact with their mother if she has not mistreated the children. Mr. Phipps stated Ms. Fox did not respond after Taylor gave her the note and stated again that Ms. Fox still lives with Mr. Kautz. 

Throughout the visit, Mr. Phipps continued to express his frustration with the Court, police, and this agency regarding this investigation. 

Worker inquired about counseling for the children. Mr. Phipps stated Taylor is on a waiting list with Andrew Gergerly. Mr. Phipps stated he went to Arundel Lodge but it did not look "child friendly." Worker asked if he was interested in in-home counseling. Mr. Phipps said he was.    
'
